  "song": {
    "name": "YAMS Script Demo",
    "author": "Per Jonsson (built via MCP with Claude)",
    "description": "Demonstration project for YAMS control scripts on the Mod Matrix (control-script Step 2 / S2.4). YAMS is a small expression language: instead of scalar amount x source, any Mod Matrix slot can run a script whose `out` value becomes the modulation offset - evaluated per voice and per control block in real time. The project has ONE instrument (\"YAMS Script Demo\") with 8 scripted routings, each showing different language features (macros like velocity/mod_wheel, context like age, stateful functions lag/phasor/sah/slew, white noise via white, math, ternaries), plus an automation lane that sweeps the vibrato depth. An 8-beat bassline loop (112 BPM) plays so the modulation is audible. Open the fx button on a Mod Matrix row in the patch editor to view/edit the scripts.",
    "patterns": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "name": "YAMS Demo Riff",
        "description": "8-beat bassline riff in A minor (A1-G2), 112 BPM, looped 0->8. Velocity is deliberately varied (58-122) so the velocity-driven scripts are audible: hard hits (118/122) open the filter and light up the resonance wobble, soft ones (58-68) leave it dark. Longer notes (E2 on beat 2, C2 on beat 6) give the age-based auto-pan and tremolo room to sweep. The pattern also carries the automation lane module:lfo:2:depth (0->1->0, S-curve) that swells the vibrato depth in and out each loop.",
